# The TUI image builds with the repository root as its context, because that
# module replaces the shared client module with a path (../client). Docker sends
# the whole context, and only .dockerignore applies to it — .gitignore does not —
# so keep it small. Other images build from their own subdirectory and use the
# .dockerignore in it.
#
# .env* must never enter the build context: the TUI image builds from the root,
# and that file is where the production stacks' secrets live (JWT_SECRET,
# TOKEN_ENCRYPTION_KEY, POSTGRES_PASSWORD). BuildKit only sends what a COPY
# needs, but the classic builder transfers the whole context, and a remote/cloud
# buildx builder sends it to a third party — so keep the secrets out of scope
# entirely (the three sub-directory files do the same).
.git
.github
.env
.env.*
backend
frontend
statement_parser
scripts
docs
# The TUI image only COPYs client/ and tui/; the MCP module is not part of any
# root-context build.
mcp
**/node_modules
**/coverage.out
**/cover.out
**/*.exe
**/dist
